1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,420
There have been Palestinians who have protested peacefully in the past.

2
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:09,860
Why is that voice not louder? Why does that voice not have more influence here?

3
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:17,100
I would ask your producers and I would ask other mainstream media producers why they don't amplify

4
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:23,460
those voices much more. The history of Palestinian nonviolent movement is robust and far greater than

5
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:28,360
any of these episodes, and yet it doesn't get the same amount of attention. In 2018,

6
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:36,040
Palestinian youth in Gaza organized the largest civil society protest. 20,000 to 40,000 Palestinians

7
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:42,380
marched peacefully every single week in the Great March of Return, demanding the right to return to

8
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:47,140
their homelands in an end of the siege. They were shot down like birds by Israeli snipers.

9
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:52,900
Mum, there was no coverage of them. The boycott divestment sanctions movement takes inspiration

10
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:59,400
from the anti-apartheid movement against South Africa, and yet that is maligned and castigated

11
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:05,980
as being violent, even though that is the quintessential form of nonviolent resistance.

12
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:12,940
In 2011 and 12, civilians boarded flotillas to break the siege on Gaza, and they were commandeered

13
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:19,300
by eight Israeli naval commandos. Where was the coverage of that? This is not about how Palestinians,

14
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:24,580
whether or not they resist peacefully or violently. This is about the right of Palestinians to resist at

15
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:30,100
all, and it really is the responsibility of media, of international diplomatic capital.

